  "ingredients": [
    "1 pound beef top sirloin steak",
    "0.25 cup soy sauce",
    "2 tablespoons white sugar",
    "2 tablespoons cornstarch",
    "0.5 teaspoon ground ginger",
    "3 tablespoons vegetable oil, divided",
    "1 red onion, cut into 1-inch squares",
    "1 green bell pepper, cut into 1-inch squares",
    "2 tomatoes, cut into wedges"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Slice steak into 1/2-inch thick slices across the grain.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/zaYSU5w_1N06eVz6RjE1Irl-k1U=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/172704-ChinesePepperSteak-ddmfs-step1-4x3-2b0f140622a7483c80bc5cd37171e201.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/172704/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk together soy sauce, sugar, cornstarch, and ginger in a bowl until the sugar has dissolved and the mixture is smooth. Place steak slices into the marinade, and stir until well-coated.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/t2T2NOZpXXq4jOZPOuBtJ1BZ63o=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/172704-ChinesePepperSteak-ddmfs-step2b-4x3-5a3c4e67b7954b51ab91cb82296f866a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/172704/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat 1 tablespoon vegetable oil in a wok or large skillet over medium-high heat, and cook steak strips in batches in hot oil so as not to crowd the pan. Cook and stir until well-browned, about 3 minutes, and remove steak from the wok to a bowl. Repeat with remaining steak, adding more oil as needed, and set the cooked meat aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/XE_DQFlTAePx5ND6Mz524EbeMyM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/172704-ChinesePepperSteak-ddmfs-step3-4x3-2c1364b88b27489199cbfe3afb234df4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/172704/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Return cooked steak strips to the hot wok, and stir in onion. Toss steak and onion together until onion begins to soften, about 2 minutes, then stir in green pepper.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ZxFi_39DHsRAcFsss2rL9JIhPNY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/172704-ChinesePepperSteak-ddmfs-step8-4x3-1834f01c28cb46ebbe26f79a7899f146.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/172704/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook and stir the mixture until peppers have turned bright green and started to become tender, about 2 minutes more, then add tomatoes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/sxZvH4045D-I-_pCP8SZ-of2EDA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/172704-ChinesePepperSteak-ddmfs-step9-4x3-a7cd9452751447498d04f7110bba5027.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/172704/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir everything together to mix and blend flavors, and serve.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/nNbgtTe12-A9YS9Ox4D_IhmmSCQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/172704-chinese-pepper-steak-DDMFS-4x3-5e58e36f7885463799f1267671c8f066.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/172704/step_06.webp"
    }
